1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:02,680
Look over here.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:04,050
JoJo!

3
00:00:04,133 --> 00:00:05,337
Tell me you're seeing this!

4
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:09,185
Just keep your guard up, Koichi,
and don't get any closer to it.

5
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,200
Hey, didn't you hear me?

6
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,040
I said look over here.

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,100
Is that his stand? JoJo!

8
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:28,634
Look at the coat rack!

9
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:32,475
The killer is here, and he's
trying to take the jacket!

10
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:35,100
Ah, good grief.

11
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:37,948
This would be when he
comes to get his suit.

12
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:40,540
Our evidence!

13
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:43,010
Wait!

14
00:00:43,093 --> 00:00:44,640
We can't go blindly after it.

15
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,440
What is his power?

16
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:56,968
Watch out, it's gonna blow!

17
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:02,600
I don't know.

18
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,210
What the?

19
00:02:27,293 --> 00:02:28,217
The owner blew up!

20
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:29,937
The killer has a bomb stand!

21
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,440
It all makes sense now.

22
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,080
This is how he got Shigechi! Oh, God.

23
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:37,026
That's why we couldn't
find his body anywhere.

24
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:41,360
He's getting away!

25
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:44,600
Calm down, Koichi. Let him go. Huh?

26
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,577
What do you mean, let him go?

27
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:47,980
You can't be serious!

28
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:49,613
If we go after him now,

29
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,337
we might actually have a shot at catching

30
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:53,897
the bastard who murdered
Reimi and Shigechi!

31
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:56,897
We need to observe the situation
before making our move.

32
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,620
Be patient, Koichi.

33
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:02,040
Do you even hear yourself?

34
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,400
Not gonna lie.

35
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:06,497
Getting a look at that name
tag would have been a big help.

36
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:10,760
But given that jacket's size, we
know he's about 175 centimeters tall.

37
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,857
What's more, he's an
unmarried office worker.

38
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:18,175
If he were married, he wouldn't need
to come here to get a button fixed.

39
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:21,000
He's between the ages of 25 and 35.

40
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,897
And from the look of the
jacket, he's pretty damn rich.

41
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:28,117
The jacket's unique fabric and styling
tell us he tends to wear designer clothing,

42
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:30,260
even without a good look at him.

43
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:33,357
This info alone just narrowed
our target down big time.

44
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,137
You know, that does make sense.

45
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:38,097
Wait a second, we can't just
stay here sitting on our hands!

46
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:39,997
The guy is a cold-blooded killer!

47
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:44,020
I want to chase him as much as
you do, but we have to stay put.

48
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,594
The bomb stand is somewhere over there.

49
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,840
It's still here?

50
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,116
Where do you see it?

51
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:58,500
I haven't seen it yet,
but I know it's here.

52
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:01,179
Let's make our way out of the door.

53
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:02,450
Slowly.

54
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:03,996
Wait, you just know?

55
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,397
But how is that possible?

56
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:08,397
There's no way you could know its
location if you haven't seen it.

57
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:12,357
He's not the kind of killer to bomb and
run after only offing that shop owner.

58
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,457
Just think about it.

59
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:16,657
If he was, his killing spree
would have ended a long time ago.

60
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:19,152
He doesn't like to leave behind evidence.

61
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:22,211
Which means he intends to take us out too.

62
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:27,757
I understand that, but don't you think
you're being a teensy bit overcautious?

63
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,677
If you're wrong about this
and his stand isn't here,

64
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:33,819
our murderer and evidence
could be long gone by now!

65
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:35,317
Listen, Koichi.

66
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,518
Observing involves far more
than just looking around.

67
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:41,057
It means scrutinizing everything.

68
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:44,140
You don't simply listen, you concentrate.

69
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:49,000
Otherwise, we'll die in this room.

70
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:53,337
I don't like what he was implying.

71
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:56,417
My reverb is more than strong
enough to keep us safe.

72
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,618
It's matured a lot since it emerged.

73
00:04:58,900 --> 00:04:59,730
Maybe Mr.

74
00:04:59,813 --> 00:05:02,015
Jotaro just doesn't take me seriously.

75
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:05,660
Well, if you asked me, that
dumb bomb stand is long gone.

76
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,256
I mean, we'd have to be total
numb nuts not to see it.

77
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,020
Over here!

78
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,700
He was right!

79
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,157
It was here all along!

80
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,037
It'll explode if I keep touching it!

81
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,320
Star Platinum!

82
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:36,960
Damn, it's tough.

83
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:40,593
I knocked it to shit, and the
thing's still in one piece.

84
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:43,180
I think it's gonna blow!

85
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,636
Star Platinum, bring forth the world!

86
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:49,617
I'd like to end this
before things get ugly,

87
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:52,229
so I'm disposing of
you right here and now.

88
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:12,810
It's gone.

89
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:15,337
You must have stopped
time and finished it off.

90
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,596
Bet you didn't see that one
coming, did you, murderer?

91
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:29,600
Anyone who dares pursue
Yoshikage Kira must be destroyed.

92
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:31,920
I'll blow them to little pieces.

93
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:36,891
They think they've won, but once Deadly
Queen's heart attack finds its prey,

94
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:39,440
it won't rest until its target is dead.

95
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:47,920
There's no way!

96
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:50,817
Not even Star Platinum had
enough power to destroy it,

97
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:52,717
which means it's practically invincible!

98
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:53,630
Damn it!

99
00:06:53,713 --> 00:06:54,773
Stay behind me, Koichi.

100
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,000
It hasn't taken any damage!

101
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,097
Nothing we do seems to
face this thing whatsoever!

102
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:15,920
I can see that. Get back.

103
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:19,737
You've been hitting it so
hard you're starting to bleed,

104
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,917
but it still doesn't have
a single scratch on it.

105
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,118
For the last time, get back, Koichi.

106
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:32,777
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

107
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:35,337
It'll explode and take
us along for the ride.

108
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,949
You have to get rid of it.

109
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:57,020
Look over here!

110
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:59,300
Good freaking grief.

111
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:00,797
This is a first for me.

112
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,697
That Stan's resilience is insane.

113
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:06,117
The way this is going, my confidence
will break before it does.

114
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,580
What now, Mr. Jotaro?

115
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:10,117
We're not going to be able
to hold out for much longer.

116
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,717
You're still too close for comfort.

117
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,277
I'm going to destroy this
alarm clock from hell.

118
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,417
I beg you, you have to listen to me.

119
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,137
When a stand's controlled from a distance,

120
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:20,377
it only wields a fraction
of its full power.

121
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:23,617
Look at the way it charges and
the intensity of its explosions.

122
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:26,337
Its owner has to be nearby
fueling it with energy.

123
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:27,857
There's no other explanation.

124
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:28,920
At most 15.

125
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:32,672
No, based on what we've seen,
the killer's 10 meters away.

126
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:33,630
And?

127
00:08:33,713 --> 00:08:34,754
What do you mean, and?

128
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:38,040
It's 10 meters and Reverb
has a range of 50 meters.

129
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,594
I can find that prick.

130
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:41,037
Don't you move.

131
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:43,380
Koichi, just leave it be.

132
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:47,856
You have one job, and it's to focus
on protecting yourself with Reverb.

133
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:49,811
Nothing else matters now.

134
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,947
You're letting him get away?

135
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:54,000
The guy's long gone, Koichi.

136
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:57,517
That means we're dealing
with a long-range stand.

137
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:01,157
Trust me, I've seen enough of these
to know what I'm talking about.

138
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,400
Over here!

139
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:05,897
Its movements are too simple
for a short-range stand.

140
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,817
He's seen enough of them to know?

141
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,257
Is he off his rocker?

142
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:13,017
We're going up against an incredibly
powerful long-range stand.

143
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,747
The user has to be close by.

144
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:16,400
I knew Mr.

145
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,402
Jotaro didn't take me seriously.

146
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:20,913
But I'll show him how much I've matured.

147
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,941
I'll find the killer and
finish him off by myself.

148
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:27,620
Ten meter range.

149
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,520
There, I found him.

150
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,664
And he has the jacket with him.

151
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:40,900
What's going on?

152
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,220
He's too far away.

153
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:44,479
That's much farther than 50 meters.

154
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:46,260
He's still going.

155
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,680
Now he's outside Reverb's range.

156
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:51,437
Does that mean the killer
really has the ability

157
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:54,049
to control such a
powerful stand from afar?

158
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,190
Impossible.

159
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,760
Over here! What?

160
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:11,160
Oh no, it's aiming at me!

161
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:12,160
Now I get it.

162
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:16,157
For some reason, the bomb stand is drawn
to whichever object it senses is hottest.

163
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:19,769
That would explain the range
and why it's still so powerful.

164
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:21,844
Use Reverb to protect yourself.

165
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,337
Stopping time is useless at that distance.

166
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,740
Oh crap, I can't.

167
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:31,420
I sent Reverb 50 meters away
to track down the killer.

168
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,080
Sorry, I didn't listen.

169
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,020
Good freaking grief, kid.

170
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,220
Star Platinum, once more the world!

171
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:52,037
It attacked the shop owner first
because of the hot liquid in his cup.

172
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:54,717
Compared to that, our
body heat didn't register.

173
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:58,565
But in Koichi's case, his frustration
increased his temperature.

174
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:02,580
If it detects something hotter,
then it moves on to that.

175
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:05,240
Enough, time resume.

176
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:10,820
I was right.

177
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:14,137
Since it's drawn to the highest
temperature it can detect,

178
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,777
it's making a beeline for me.

179
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:18,240
What is he planning? All right.

180
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:21,217
If body temperature is all
it takes to trigger this,

181
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,476
then fire should be more than enough.

182
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,080
This power!

183
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,120
Mr. Chotaro!

184
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,110
Mr.

185
00:11:51,193 --> 00:11:52,023
Chotaro!

186
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:01,740
How could I let this happen? Mr.

187
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:03,625
Chotaro, this is all my fault!

188
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:09,037
All because I went after that bastard!

189
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,877
This wouldn't have happened if he hadn't

190
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,548
had to stop time and
save me with that fire!

191
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:25,620
That was not the sensation
of human flesh exploding.

192
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,320
Over here.

193
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,960
Ah! Ah!

194
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,340
It's gonna kill us!

195
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,860
It's just too powerful!

196
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:51,960
It's like Mr.

197
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,097
Jotaro was saying.

198
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:56,697
If it detects a temperature hotter than
body heat, it goes after that first.

199
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:58,020
Over here!

200
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:00,517
Now's our chance to make a break for it.

201
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:02,537
I need to find a way to call Josuke.

202
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,640
He'll be able to fix Mr. Jotaro.

203
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:06,987
I just need to find a phone!

204
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:13,520
Oh, of course!

205
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,840
It's the kitchen!

206
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:17,057
Lots of ways to start a fire in here!

207
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:20,357
I'll buy some time, and then
we'll escape through that door.

208
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,270
A phone!

209
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:27,490
Wait!

210
00:13:27,573 --> 00:13:29,057
You have got to be kidding me!

211
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:30,493
This isn't a gas stove!

212
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:33,097
Why the hell does this house
have to have an electric one?

213
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:35,257
I bet it's gonna take forever to get hot.

214
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:37,060
Aw, come on! The oven, too?

215
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:40,840
What do I do now?

216
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:43,795
I bet that kettle has hot water in it!

217
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:45,320
Try and fight me now!

218
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:49,620
Ah! It's empty!

219
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,820
Get over here!

220
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:13,320
Calm down.

221
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,260
It's like Mr. Jotaro said.

222
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,500
I need to carefully observe. Focus.

223
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:19,349
This thing has a weakness.

224
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,560
I never noticed it until now.

225
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:26,655
You're really starting to piss me off.

226
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:31,857
You're nothing but a repulsive murderer,
a stain on the fabric of humanity.

227
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,857
Why should a Dark like
you have the satisfaction

228
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:36,175
of watching me flee and beg for mercy?

229
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:38,517
Shouldn't the roles be reversed?

230
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:42,397
I already know that I can get out of
this mess alive, so for the life of me,

231
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:45,377
I can't figure out why I'm just standing
here like a wimpy little bitch baby?

232
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,166
with a bad case of the shits.

233
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:49,757
I've had this all wrong
from the beginning!

234
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:53,140
The one who should be
running away is you, dick!

235
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:55,060
This ends once and for all!

236
00:14:56,860 --> 00:14:59,517
You're unrelenting in your
pursuit of thermal energy,

237
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:01,600
but that's also your shortcoming!

238
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:04,587
Your inability to stuff
will be your undoing!

239
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:09,214
You're gonna pay for your crimes, so
consider this the first installment!

240
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:14,317
It's been three minutes
since I made my escape.

241
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:17,977
I don't know what's transpired at
the shoe store in the meantime,

242
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:21,117
but no matter how strong my
opponent There's one thing.

243
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:25,440
I'm certain of heart attack is the
ultimate stand and has no weaknesses

244
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:29,940
It'll find and destroy
any target without fail.

245
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:35,715
Okay, with that thing out of the way,
all that's left is to call Josuke!

246
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:38,945
He should have made it
home from school by now.

247
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:51,659
At least that pest is
distracted for the time being.

248
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:53,477
I don't think it'll fool it forever,

249
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:56,617
but the sizzle should keep it busy
long enough to make a phone call.

250
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:57,530
Lucky for me,

251
00:15:57,620 --> 00:16:01,777
the little jackass is as gullible as
a donkey chasing a hanging carrot.

252
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:03,920
And that's your stance fatal flaw.

253
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:06,018
Gashkata residents.

254
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:08,101
Josuke, it's Koichi, I need help!

255
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:11,237
Jotaro's hurt, I don't
think he's gonna make it!

